Doing the computation, we obtain $$n=(\gamma^2-r^4) \, \omega^4+2 \, r^2 \, \omega_0^2 \, \beta \, (\gamma^2-r^2) \, \omega^2+r^4 \, \omega_0^4 \, (\gamma^2-1),$$
where $\beta = 2 \, \xi^2 -1$.
The resultant $R$ of $n(\omega, \gamma)$ and $\frac{\partial n}{\partial \omega}(\omega, \gamma)$ with respect to $\omega$ is then defined by
