\subsubsection{Functional relevance}

From \textbf{Figure \ref{feature}}, it can be observed that the distributions of generated and natural sequences are similar in shape, location, and width across most features, indicating that the model effectively simulates the distribution of natural sequences in these physicochemical properties. The closeness of their medians further emphasizes the functional relevance of the model. This also verifies the effectiveness of the CVAE encoder in mapping data to the latent space, as the training result shows in \textbf{Figure} \ref{normal}. In \textbf{Figure \ref{matrix}}, high similarity along the diagonal further supports the successful alignment between matching text and sequences. Lower similarity in off-diagonal areas indicates the  ability to distinguish non-matching pairs, demonstrating the strong text-sequence alignment capabilities of BioAligner. Additionally, a high Textual Semantic Fidelity scores is an indicator of strong alignment between input descriptions and generated sequences. With CMADiff achieving a semantic similarity score of 0.94, this result emphasizes the effectiveness of the BioAligner module in maintaining semantic relevance.

