\subsubsection{Code Generation}

Many inference calls are made through the pipeline to generate responses. While each inference may have a specialized instruction prompt to guide task-specific behavior, we implement the same system prompt for all inference steps. The system prompt is a key parameter that aligns the LLM with the intended task by assigning a role to guide its behavior toward generating expected responses \cite{BuildLLMs}. For LASSI-EE, the system prompt suggests to the LLM that it is a ``expert'' C++/CUDA engineer with the goal of refactoring code to improve energy efficiency. We found that providing the same system prompt across the pipeline provided consistency across LLM responses and established good performance in generated codes. This standard system prompt is listed in Table \ref{tab:systemprompt}.

