\subsubsection{Code Refactor Planning}\label{sec:planning} 
The LLM is provided with the source code and prompted to summarize its expected functionality and analyze the code in terms of the refactoring task, guided by the same system prompt of Table \ref{tab:systemprompt}. In this scenario, we include the complete background programming and optimization knowledge to ensure the model has as much detail as possible when reviewing the code. 

During this final step of Stage 2, the LLM is prompted to develop a refactoring plan of the source code or prior code revision, which could be the zero-shot optimized code. This refactoring plan is central to the LASSI-EE overall prompting strategy by having the LLM effectively synthesize the context information curated through its self-summarizations and prepare itself to generate energy-efficient code in the next pipeline stage. Here, the LLM is instructed through a five-step process to read the context, analyze the original source code, identify inefficiencies in the provided code, and propose a refactoring plan that considers the computing system characteristics and best practice optimizations. No code should be generated during this inference. The detailed refactoring plan prompt is listed in Table \ref{tab:refactorplanprompt}.

Importantly, the instructions here include the prior review of the \emph{source code} along with its analysis of the revised code, when provided. This prompt structure encourages the model to keep some focus on the original code, which can be especially useful if any functionality in a code revision steers away from the source's original expectation.

