One may
wonder whether CIDM channels could be partitioned also in a different
fashion. The answer is yes, several other partitions are possible. For example,
one could transmit signal $u_g$ and move the slew-rate limiter and the scheduler
to the succeeding channel. This would, however, mean that properties of single
CIDM channels depend on the properties of both predecessor and successor gate,
which complicates the process of channel characterization
and parametrization based on design parameters.

