where $e=(u,v,t)$ represents an edge, $u$ and $v$ are the source and target nodes, $t$ is the timestamp of the edge, $S$ is the set of edges associated with $e$, $u'$ and $v'$ are nodes different from $u$ and $v$, $t'$ is the timestamp of the other edges, and $M_{u,v,t}$ are the relevant edges of $e$. Following that, each edge feature at graph layer $l+1$ is updated by aggregating its own features with its linked nodes and the mean value of aggregated features from other relevant edges as follows.

\begin{align*}
