\noindent \textbf{Impact of Transaction:} Learning-based methods, due to the reliance on large transaction volumes and the absence of code analysis, also performed poorly. To further evaluate the impact of transaction volume, we analyzed the transaction distribution within our Rug Pull dataset. Our findings indicate that 84$\%$ of Rug Pull tokens have more than 100 transactions, whereas only 3.4$\%$ of tokens have fewer than 10 transactions. In fact, Rug Pull tokens typically have high transaction volumes to create the illusion of active trading and ensure sufficient profits before the scam, which are available for transaction analysis.
