Creating multiple-choice questions for this task is challenging. Annotators must understand different ToM abilities, find relevant moments in short films, and write clear questions. Making good distractors is also difficult because humans often create distractors that models can easily guess without seeing the video context, as observed by \citet{guo-etal-2023-desiq} in other multimodal social understanding datasets. 

To address these challenges, we conducted two pilot annotation rounds (see Appendix \ref{sec:pilot}) before launching the main annotation phase. Findings from the pilots helped us refine our pipeline to address the cognitive demands of ToM question creation, reduce annotation biases, and ensure question quality. The final methodology included carefully structured annotation phases, refined guidelines, and a custom-built platform to support robust distractor generation.

